    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d787">

                <pb facs="1074" n="1064" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1064"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Nanking Embassy Files, Lot F79, 820 Surplus
                    Property: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Embassy in China
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-01-07T16:00:00+08:00">January 7, 1946—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. From Johnson, Foreign Liquidation Commission, Shanghai. <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Soong has stated China wants only the FEA stockpile (in reply to
                            Embassy’s telegram No. 10, January 5, 11 a.m.) at Calcutta. India–Burma
                            Theatre has been so advised by radio.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[Johnson] <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
